{"task_id": "HumanEval/13", "solution": "def greatest_common_divisor(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" Return a greatest common divisor of two integers a and b.\n    This implementation uses the Euclidean algorithm.\n    >>> greatest_common_divisor(3, 5)\n    1\n    >>> greatest_common_divisor(25, 15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert inputs to their absolute values, as GCD is typically positive.\n    # This prepares them for the Euclidean algorithm.\n    a = abs(a)\n    b = abs(b)\n\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return a"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/13", "solution": "def greatest_common_divisor(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" Return a greatest common divisor of two integers a and b\n    >>> greatest_common_divisor(3, 5)\n    1\n    >>> greatest_common_divisor(25, 15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    # Implementation using Euclidean algorithm\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return a"}
