{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "def largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n.\n    For n=1, it returns 1 as per the design's edge case handling.\n    >>> largest_divisor(15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Iterate downwards from n-1 to 1 to find the largest proper divisor.\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return i"}
