{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "def is_prime(n):\n    \"\"\"Return true if a given number is prime, and false otherwise.\n\n    Args:\n        n (int): The number to check for primality\n\n    Returns:\n        bool: True if n is prime, False otherwise\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> is_prime(6)\n        False\n        >>> is_prime(101)\n        True\n        >>> is_prime(11)\n        True\n        >>> is_prime(13441)\n        True\n        >>> is_prime(61)\n        True\n        >>> is_prime(4)\n        False\n        >>> is_prime(1)\n        False\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    # Check for divisors from 3 up to the square root of n, incrementing by 2\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 2\n    return True"}
