{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\n\ndef poly(xs: list, x: float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\n    return xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[1] * x^2 + .... xs[n] * x^n\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\n\n\ndef _has_even_coefficients(xs: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the coefficient list has an even number of elements.\"\"\"\n    return len(xs) % 2 == 0\n\n\ndef _has_nonzero_largest(xs: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Verifies the largest coefficient is non-zero.\"\"\"\n    return xs[-1] != 0\n\n\ndef _validate_coefficients(xs: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates coefficients meet zero-finding constraints.\"\"\"\n    if not xs:\n        return False\n    return _has_even_coefficients(xs) and _has_nonzero_largest(xs)\n\n\ndef find_zero(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs are coefficients of a polynomial.\n    find_zero find x such that poly(x) = 0.\n    find_zero returns only only zero point, even if there are many.\n    Moreover, find_zero only takes list xs having even number of coefficients\n    and largest non zero coefficient as it guarantees\n    a solution.\n    >>> round(find_zero([1, 2]), 2) # f(x) = 1 + 2x\n    -0.5\n    >>> round(find_zero([-6, 11, -6, 1]), 2) # (x - 1) * (x - 2) * (x - 3) = -6 + 11x - 6x^2 + x^3\n    1.0\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_coefficients(xs):\n        raise ValueError(\"Polynomial does not meet zero-finding constraints: even coefficient count and non-zero largest coefficient are required.\")\n\n    low = -1.0\n    high = 1.0\n    # Expand interval until poly(low) and poly(high) have opposite signs.\n    # This loop is guaranteed to terminate for odd-degree polynomials.\n    while poly(xs, low) * poly(xs, high) >= 0:\n        low *= 2.0\n        high *= 2.0\n\n    epsilon = 1e-7\n    max_iterations = 100\n\n    for _ in range(max_iterations):\n        mid = (low + high) / 2\n        p_mid = poly(xs, mid)\n\n        if abs(p_mid) < epsilon:\n            return mid\n\n        p_low = poly(xs, low)\n        if p_low * p_mid < 0:  # Root is in [low, mid]\n            high = mid\n        else:  # Root is in [mid, high]\n            low = mid\n\n    # Return the current midpoint if max iterations are reached.\n    return (low + high) / 2\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "import math\n\n\ndef poly(xs: list, x: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\n    Returns xs[0] + xs[1] * x + ... + xs[n] * x^n.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\n\n\ndef find_zero(xs: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"find_zero finds x such that poly(x) = 0 for polynomial coefficients xs. It returns a single zero point, assuming the input constraints are met.\"\"\"\n    # Coefficients for the derivative polynomial P'(x)\n    # P'(x) = xs[1] + 2*xs[2]*x + ... + n*xs[n]*x^(n-1)\n    xs_prime = [i * xs[i] for i in range(1, len(xs))]\n\n    x_candidate = 0.0  # Initial guess for the root\n    tolerance = 1e-6\n    max_iterations = 100\n\n    for _ in range(max_iterations):\n        y = poly(xs, x_candidate)\n\n        if abs(y) < tolerance:\n            return x_candidate\n\n        y_prime = poly(xs_prime, x_candidate)\n        \n        # Proceed with division assuming y_prime will not be problematic as per design.\n        x_candidate = x_candidate - y / y_prime\n\n    return x_candidate # Return the best estimate if not converged within iterations"}
