{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "import itertools\n\ndef _validate_input(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the input list has at least three elements.\n    Returns True if valid, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    return len(l) >= 3\n\ndef _calculate_sum(triplet: tuple) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of three integers in a given triplet.\n    Returns the sum of the elements.\"\"\"\n    return triplet[0] + triplet[1] + triplet[2]\n\ndef _generate_triplets(l: list) -> itertools.combinations:\n    \"\"\"Generates all possible three-element combinations from the input list.\n    Yields tuples of three distinct elements.\"\"\"\n    return itertools.combinations(l, 3)\n\ndef triples_sum_to_zero(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    triples_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are three distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n\n    >>> triples_sum_to_zero([1, 3, 5, 0])\n    False\n    >>> triples_sum_to_zero([1, 3, -2, 1])\n    True\n    >>> triples_sum_to_zero([1, 2, 3, 7])\n    False\n    >>> triples_sum_to_zero([2, 4, -5, 3, 9, 7])\n    True\n    >>> triples_sum_to_zero([1])\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_input(l):\n        return False\n\n    for triplet in _generate_triplets(l):\n        if _calculate_sum(triplet) == 0:\n            return True\n\n    return False"}
